      "content": "2.1 Location and Extent"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Madhya Pradesh geography encompasses physical divisions, river systems, climate, forests, wildlife, and mineral resources.",
        "Prominent physical regions include the Satpura Range and Vindhyan Range.",
        "Key river systems driving the state's drainage are the Narmada River and Chambal River.",
        "Rich biodiversity is preserved through extensive forest cover, national parks, wildlife sanctuaries, and biosphere reserves."
      ],
