    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "53i6vul",
      "content": "Madhya Pradesh, meaning 'Middle Province' or 'Heart of India,' is geographically situated in the central part of India. It is aptly called the 'Heart of India' because it lies at the geographical center of the country. The state lies between 21°6' N to 26°30' N latitude and 74°9' E to 82°48' E longitude."
    },
