    {
      "id": "53ofbxd",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Chambal River"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4kgwepc",
      "content": "The Chambal originates from Janapav Hills near Indore and flows northward through the Malwa Plateau and Bundelkhand before joining the Yamuna in Uttar Pradesh. The Chambal valley is known for its ravines (beehad) which historically provided shelter to dacoits. Major dams on Chambal are Gandhi Sagar Dam, Rana Pratap Sagar Dam (in Rajasthan), and Jawahar Sagar Dam. The National Chambal Sanctuary is an important wildlife sanctuary on the Chambal."
    },
