    {
      "id": "liizgyl",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2.4 Climate of Madhya Pradesh"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "q0qy2mq",
      "content": "Madhya Pradesh has a tropical monsoon climate. The state experiences three distinct seasons: summer (March-June), monsoon (July-October), and winter (November-February). The average annual rainfall ranges from 800mm in the western parts to over 1600mm in the eastern parts."
    },
