    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9bitpc9",
      "content": "The highest temperature is usually recorded in Gwalior and Morena districts, which can touch 48°C in summer. The coolest parts of the state are the Pachmarhi plateau and the forested areas of Balaghat and Mandla. Pachmarhi records the lowest temperatures in winter, sometimes going below 5°C."
    },
    {
      "id": "tu2p8bo",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2.5 Forests and Wildlife"
    },
    {
      "id": "28xn0va",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Forest Cover"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "n2s2o9x",
      "content": "Madhya Pradesh has the highest forest cover among all Indian states in terms of absolute area. As per the India State of Forest Report 2021, MP has approximately 77,482 sq km of forest cover, which is about 25.14% of its total geographical area. The state is called the 'Tiger State of India' as it has the highest number of tigers in India."
    },
